  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordination of the work of Caritas throughout Latin America and the Caribbean Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SELACC is the Secretariat of the Latin American and Caribbean Caritas organisations.  Its role is to strengthen the regional structure of Caritas and coordinate the work of Caritas throughout Latin American and the Caribbean, enabling a strategic approach to addressing root causes of inequality across the region and promoting respect for human rights, human dignity, and peacebuilding as well as providing a platform for learning and exchange, training in best practice on issues such as stewardship, gender equity and accountability .  SELACC liaises with the Department for Justice and Solidarity of the Latin American Bishops Conference and the two organisations have developed a closer working relationship over the last few years.  This project will continue CAFOD&apos;s support to SELACC as it enters a new strategic planning period.  In 2014 it will define its strategic plan for 2015-2019.    CAFOD anticipates maintaining its support to the regional coordination of the Caritas network for the period of the new strategic plan.</narrative>
  </description>
